changes.change:
A trigger for non-convergence, with Nathan deciding whether to continue. Any one of these ends the loop with a DECISION NEEDED:
- distinct confirmed required defects fail to fall by at least half from the previous round;
- most of a round's findings sit in text the last repair added;
- time or tokens pass twice the estimate Nathan approved.
The DECISION NEEDED gives the trend, the open findings with path and likelihood, and options.

Resume only at checkpoints:
- mode boundaries (template rule 2, D21-D);
- before the first Notion write, by restarting from X0.2;
- each post-merge step, started fresh from main.
A session lost inside the Notion write window is a stop. No 'any step can run in a new session' claim.

